		<div class="texto-blog">					
		<p>In this article we will see <strong>How to configure codeigniter 3 framework</strong>.</p>
		
		<h2 class="texto-title-blog">How to configure the base_url?</h2>

		{{ include('inc/ad_defect.html.twig') }} 
		
		<p>First we will go to <code>nameProject/application/config/config.php</code>, where we have this empty variable.</p>
		

	
		<pre class="text-code">
		<code class="">
	$config['base_url'] = '';
		</code>
		</pre>

		
		<p>Now what we will do is set this url, by the url of your local server or domain.</p>
		

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code class="">
	$config['base_url'] = 'http://localhost/your_app/';
		</code>
		</pre>

		<h2 class="texto-title-blog">How do we load resources?</h2>		

		
		<p>Now we will automatically load all the resources that we want to use in our application in <code>nameApp/application/config/autoload.php</code>, or we can also load it in the <strong>constructor</strong>.</p>
		

		<pre class="text-code">
		<code class="">
	//we load all the libraries to use		
	$autoload['libraries'] = array('database', 'form_validation', 'email', 'session', 'pagination');

	//we load all the helpers to use
	$autoload['helper'] = array('url' ,'security');
		</code>
		</pre>		

